        "title": "VO2max, Lactate Threshold, and Aerobic Capacity",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Three physiological variables predict endurance performance: VO2max (oxygen ceiling), lactate threshold (the fraction of that ceiling you can sustain), and running/cycling economy (efficiency). Understanding what each is, what limits it, and how it's trained is the foundation of endurance sports science."
    },
